## Scope of the two licenses

Original application source code is additionally offered under the MIT license
(see LICENSE-MIT), at the recipient's option. This is a choice of licenses for
that code, not a requirement to comply with both licenses at once.

- Original program code, including TypeScript/TSX, CSS, HTML, Python, shell
  scripts, build configuration, and automated test code: CC BY-SA 4.0 OR MIT.
- Ars Magica game content, including the records under `data/`, published
  character fixtures under `test/golden/`, copied or adapted rules text, and
  game-content portions of generated sheets: CC BY-SA 4.0 only.
- Project prose documentation: CC BY-SA 4.0, unless explicitly marked otherwise.
- Third-party dependencies and other separately attributed material: their own
  licenses, which this project does not replace.

Location and file extension do not override these distinctions. In particular,
the MIT option does not extend to Ars Magica content embedded in a source file
or a test fixture. Bundling code and game data together does not make the game
data available under MIT. Preserve attribution and license notices for each.

LICENSE-MIT is the standard MIT text for eligible original code; it is not an
alternative license for every file in this repository.

## Player-created records and generated output

Using the application does not by itself grant this project rights in a
player's original character, campaign notes, or other contributions, or publish
them under either project license. Embedded licensed game content retains its
existing terms. Adaptations of licensed material must comply with CC BY-SA 4.0
when shared. Generated sheets should preserve the game-content attribution,
license link, indication of changes, and applicable trademark statements.

Official licensing and trademark conditions:
https://atlas-games.com/arsmagica/openars

